  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Model-Based Diffusion for Trajectory Optimization",
      "bbox": [
        116.5459976196289,
        101.16837310791016,
        495.4570617675781,
        116.64501953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chaoyi Pan∗, Zeji Yi∗, Guanya Shi†, Guannan Qu†",
      "bbox": [
        197.5330047607422,
        160.26876831054688,
        413.9688720703125,
        170.88919067382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Carnegie Mellon University",
      "bbox": [
        250.37896728515625,
        172.96136474609375,
        361.62127685546875,
        181.867919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "{chaoyip,zejiy,guanyas,gqu}@andrew.cmu.edu",
      "bbox": [
        196.18896484375,
        184.53785705566406,
        415.85467529296875,
        192.83670043945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Abstract",
      "bbox": [
        283.7579650878906,
        223.55792236328125,
        328.2432556152344,
        234.30564880371094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Recent advances in diffusion models have demonstrated their strong capabilities in",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        247.77838134765625,
        468.12994384765625,
        256.6849365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "generating high-fidelity samples from complex distributions through an iterative",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        258.6873779296875,
        468.12921142578125,
        267.59393310546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "refinement process. Despite the empirical success of diffusion models in motion",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        269.59637451171875,
        468.1293029785156,
        278.5029296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "planning and control, the model-free nature of these methods does not leverage",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        280.50537109375,
        468.1308898925781,
        289.41192626953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "readily available model information and limits their generalization to new scenarios",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        291.41436767578125,
        468.13616943359375,
        300.3209228515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "beyond the training data (e.g., new robots with different dynamics). In this work,",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        302.3233642578125,
        469.37896728515625,
        311.22991943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we introduce Model-Based Diffusion (MBD), an optimization approach using the",
      "bbox": [
        143.5070037841797,
        313.23236083984375,
        468.1385498046875,
        322.138916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diffusion process to solve trajectory optimization (TO) problems without data.",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        324.0417175292969,
        469.8774719238281,
        333.04791259765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The key idea is to explicitly compute the score function by leveraging the model",
      "bbox": [
        143.5570068359375,
        335.0513610839844,
        468.1291198730469,
        343.9579162597656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "information in TO problems, which is why we refer to our approach as model-",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        345.8607177734375,
        469.7885437011719,
        354.8669128417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "based diffusion. Moreover, although MBD does not require external data, it",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        356.76971435546875,
        468.1310119628906,
        365.7759094238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "can be naturally integrated with data of diverse qualities to steer the diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        367.7783508300781,
        468.13067626953125,
        376.6849060058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "process. We also reveal that MBD has interesting connections to sampling-based",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        378.6873474121094,
        468.13177490234375,
        387.5939025878906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "optimization. Empirical evaluations show that MBD outperforms state-of-the-art",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        389.59637451171875,
        468.13116455078125,
        398.5029296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reinforcement learning and sampling-based TO methods in challenging contact-rich",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        400.50537109375,
        468.1361083984375,
        409.41192626953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tasks. Additionally, MBD’s ability to integrate with data enhances its versatility and",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        411.41436767578125,
        468.1361389160156,
        420.3209228515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "practical applicability, even with imperfect and infeasible data (e.g., partial-state",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        422.3233642578125,
        468.1343994140625,
        431.22991943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "demonstrations for high-dimensional humanoids), beyond the scope of standard",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        433.23236083984375,
        468.1310119628906,
        442.138916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diffusion models. Videos and codes: https://lecar-lab.github.io/mbd/",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        444.141357421875,
        459.8392639160156,
        453.1076965332031
      ],
      "direction": [
